<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan CPC tenders to buy July 1-20 fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC tenders to buy July 1-20 fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy one to two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent fuel oil for July delivery, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>CPC seeks to buy the low-pour cargoes for delivery July 1-20 to Keelung, Taichung or Shenao on a cost-and-freight basis (c-and-f).</p>
<p>The tender closes May 21 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last fuel oil purchase, CPC bought two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent fuel oil at around $117 and $120 per tonne respectively for June 1-30 and June 11-30 deliveries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 8703571)</p>
